{{!
    @template local_moodesk/admin_departments

    Department administration — list view of configured departments with edit/members/toggle actions.

    Context variables:
      * departments[]   - Array of department rows: {id, name, isactive, statuslabel, membercount,
                          plugincell {text, highlighted}, editurl, membersurl, listurl, togglelabel, sesskey}
      * hasdepartments  - True when at least one department exists
      * pluginlabel     - Heading of the column plugins add (hook department_list_columns), when one does
      * newurl          - URL to create a new department

    THE TABLE IS THE PRODUCT'S TABLE. Surface, header, row height, cell padding,
    hover, empty state and the phone treatment all come from
    components/_datatable.scss and are the same here as on every other screen.
    What belongs to this screen is which columns exist and where each one lands
    once the row becomes a card — modules/_departments.scss.

    `table-reboot` alongside `.mhd-datatable` is not optional: Moodle 5 borders
    every `th` in a table that does not carry Bootstrap's `.table`, and that rule
    is past what our stylesheet can outrank.

    Below 992px the table is painted as one card per row. The markup is the same
    at every width — one loop, one set of cells, no second copy of the row for
    phones. Changing `display` on table elements costs the table its implicit
    semantics, so each cell carries its column name as real text in a
    .mhd-cell-label, hidden by CSS wherever the header row is doing that job.
    Real text rather than a CSS ::before, because generated content is not
    reliably announced, and rather than explicit ARIA roles, because the HTML
    validator rejects role="row"/"cell" inside a table that still says
    role="table".

    Example context (json):
    {
      "pageheader": {
        "title": "Departments",
        "description": null,
        "meta": null,
        "actions": [],
        "primaryaction": {
          "label": "New Department",
          "url": "/local/moodesk/department_edit.php",
          "hasurl": true,
          "icon": "plus",
          "hasicon": true,
          "icononly": true,
          "variant": "filled",
          "attributes": [],
          "hasattributes": false
        },
        "hasactions": true
      },
      "hasdepartments": true,
      "pluginlabel": "SLA",
      "newurl": "/local/moodesk/admin/department_edit.php",
      "departments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "Support",
          "isactive": true,
          "statuslabel": "Active",
          "membercount": 5,
          "plugincell": {"text": "Global", "highlighted": false},
          "editurl": "/local/moodesk/admin/department_edit.php?id=1",
          "membersurl": "/local/moodesk/admin/department_members.php?id=1",
          "listurl": "/local/moodesk/admin/departments.php",
          "togglelabel": "Disable",
          "sesskey": "abc123"
        }
      ]
    }
}}
<div class="mhd-admin-departments">

  {{#pageheader}}{{> local_moodesk/page_header }}{{/pageheader}}

  {{#hasdepartments}}
  <div class="mhd-datatable-surface">
    {{! Four columns and a set of actions fit a laptop comfortably, but a long
        department name or a narrow window can still take the table past its
        panel — so it scrolls inside the panel rather than dropping its last
        column, exactly as every other table in the product does. Below 992px
        the rows are cards and there is nothing to scroll. }}
    <div class="mhd-datatable-scroll">
    <table class="mhd-datatable table-reboot mhd-dept-table">
      <caption class="mhd-sr-only">{{#str}} dept_table_caption, local_moodesk {{/str}}</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">{{#str}} department_name, local_moodesk {{/str}}</th>
          <th scope="col">{{#str}} ticket_status, local_moodesk {{/str}}</th>
          <th scope="col">{{#str}} dept_members_col, local_moodesk {{/str}}</th>
          {{#pluginlabel}}<th scope="col">{{pluginlabel}}</th>{{/pluginlabel}}
          {{! The actions column has no visible heading — it never had one — but
              it still needs a name for anyone navigating the table by column. }}
          <th scope="col"><span class="mhd-sr-only">{{#str}} actions, local_moodesk {{/str}}</span></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {{#departments}}
        <tr>
          {{! A row header rather than a cell: it names every other value in the
              row, which is what a screen reader repeats as it moves along them,
              and what titles the card below 992px.

              Plain text on purpose — the row's action buttons own navigation,
              so the name is a label, not a second way into the same screen.

              The entity figure is a mark, not a portrait: a department has no
              face, and a placeholder photograph would say it did. Same circle,
              same size and same left edge as the avatar on the Agents table, so
              the two screens line their names up identically. }}
          {{! The name is output with a triple-stache, deliberately.
              `format_string()` on the PHP side has already escaped it and
              applied Moodle's multilang filters; escaping it a second time here
              is what rendered a department called "Billing & Accounts" as
              "Billing &amp;amp; Accounts". A value that went through
              format_string() is output raw — that is the standard pairing, and
              every migrated table follows it for the same reason. }}
          <th scope="row" class="mhd-cell--entity mhd-dept-name">
            <span class="mhd-entity">
              <span class="mhd-entity__icon">
                <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#mhd-icon-departments"></use></svg>
              </span>
              <span class="mhd-entity__body">
                <span class="mhd-entity__name">{{{name}}}</span>
              </span>
            </span>
          </th>
          {{! No .mhd-cell-label: the pill already says Active or Archived, so
              the word "Status" beside it would be a label carrying no
              information. The column keeps its name for assistive tech through
              the header row. }}
          <td class="mhd-cell--status mhd-dept-status">
            <span class="mhd-pill {{#isactive}}mhd-pill--success{{/isactive}}{{^isactive}}mhd-pill--neutral{{/isactive}}">
              {{statuslabel}}
            </span>
          </td>
          <td class="mhd-dept-members mhd-cell-pair mhd-cell-pair--inline">
            <span class="mhd-cell-label">{{#str}} dept_members_col, local_moodesk {{/str}}</span>{{membercount}}
          </td>
          {{#pluginlabel}}
          <td class="mhd-dept-sla mhd-cell-pair mhd-cell-pair--inline">
            <span class="mhd-cell-label">{{pluginlabel}}</span>
            {{#plugincell}}
            {{#highlighted}}<span class="mhd-pill mhd-pill--info">{{text}}</span>{{/highlighted}}
            {{^highlighted}}<span class="text-muted small">{{text}}</span>{{/highlighted}}
            {{/plugincell}}
          </td>
          {{/pluginlabel}}
          <td class="mhd-cell--actions mhd-dept-actions">
            {{! Icon-only, and small rather than xsmall: 40px is a target a
                finger can hit, and three of them side by side is exactly where
                a near miss lands on the wrong one. Outlined, because three
                filled buttons per row would leave the page with no primary
                action at all.

                Each carries an aria-label AND a title — the first for anyone
                who cannot see the glyph, the second for anyone who can see it
                and still cannot place it. Nothing else in the row says what
                these do. }}
            <div class="mhd-action-group">
              <a href="{{editurl}}" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined mhd-btn--icon"
                 aria-label="{{#str}} dept_edit_heading, local_moodesk {{/str}}"
                 title="{{#str}} dept_edit_heading, local_moodesk {{/str}}">
                <svg class="mhd-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                  <use href="#mhd-icon-edit"></use>
                </svg>
              </a>
              <a href="{{membersurl}}" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined mhd-btn--icon"
                 aria-label="{{#str}} department_members, local_moodesk {{/str}}"
                 title="{{#str}} department_members, local_moodesk {{/str}}">
                <svg class="mhd-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                  <use href="#mhd-icon-users"></use>
                </svg>
              </a>
              {{! Archiving is reversible and the button says which way it goes,
                  so it is outlined like its neighbours rather than destructive.
                  The glyph follows the label: a box to file it away, an arrow
                  to bring it back. }}
              <form method="post" action="{{listurl}}">
                <input type="hidden" name="action"  value="toggle">
                <input type="hidden" name="deptid"  value="{{id}}">
                <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
                <button type="submit" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--outlined mhd-btn--icon"
                        aria-label="{{togglelabel}}" title="{{togglelabel}}">
                  <svg class="mhd-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <use href="{{#isactive}}#mhd-icon-archive{{/isactive}}{{^isactive}}#mhd-icon-restore{{/isactive}}"></use>
                  </svg>
                </button>
              </form>
            </div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        {{/departments}}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{/hasdepartments}}

  {{^hasdepartments}}
  {{! The empty state lives inside the surface, not instead of it: the panel is
      where the table would have been, so the page does not change shape when
      the last department goes. One component, the same one Agents uses. }}
  <div class="mhd-datatable-surface">
    <div class="mhd-datatable-empty">
      <div class="mhd-empty-state">
        <svg class="mhd-empty-state-icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <use href="#mhd-icon-departments"></use>
        </svg>
        <p class="mhd-empty-state-desc">{{#str}} dept_no_departments, local_moodesk {{/str}}</p>
        {{! Nothing exists yet: this is the invitation, at the default size. }}
        <a href="{{newurl}}" class="mhd-btn mhd-btn--filled">
          <svg class="mhd-btn__icon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <use href="#mhd-icon-newticket"></use>
          </svg>
          {{#str}} dept_new_heading, local_moodesk {{/str}}
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {{/hasdepartments}}

</div>
